/-! ## §1 — THE ONE DERIVED BORN TURN: five submultiples of `azimuthalTurn = 2·cutPi`. -/

/-- ★ NEW TIE. The O1 fold phase is the SIXTEENTH of the derived Born turn: `foldPhase =
    azimuthalTurn/16`. The ℍ-level half-angle amplitude root (N416) sits at `azimuthalTurn/16` on the
    fold's own return circle (N328). Never banked — O1 built `foldPhase = cutPi/8`; this welds it to
    the shared turn. Physics-words-removable: `cutPi/8 = (2·cutPi)/16`. -/
theorem foldPhase_azimuthal : foldPhase = azimuthalTurn / 16 := by
  unfold foldPhase azimuthalTurn; ring

/-- ★ NEW TIE. The O3 Cabibbo relative phase is the EIGHTH of the derived Born turn: `2·foldPhase =
    azimuthalTurn/8`. The CP-carrying phase `2P = cutPi/4` (N418) is `azimuthalTurn/8`. Never banked.
    Physics-words-removable: `2·(cutPi/8) = (2·cutPi)/8`. -/
theorem cabibbo_azimuthal : (2 : Cut) * foldPhase = azimuthalTurn / 8 := by
  unfold foldPhase azimuthalTurn; ring

/-- ★ THE FIVE-FOLD BORN-TURN THREAD. FIVE arc-O / tower quantities are submultiples of the ONE
    derived Born turn `azimuthalTurn = 2·cutPi` (N328, the fold's return surface): the O1 fold phase
    (`/16`), the O3 Cabibbo phase (`/8`), the O8 fine-structure budget (`·42`), the N359
    gravitational coupling (`·4`), and the O9 Unruh/KMS period (`/a`). The fine-structure constant,
    gravity, the CKM phase, the fold phase, and the Unruh temperature are ONE turn read five ways. -/
theorem born_turn_thread (a : Cut) :
    foldPhase = azimuthalTurn / 16
    ∧ (2 : Cut) * foldPhase = azimuthalTurn / 8
    ∧ criticalPhaseNumerator = azimuthalTurn * 42
    ∧ gravCouplingCoeff = azimuthalTurn * 4
    ∧ unruhPeriod a = azimuthalTurn / a :=
  ⟨foldPhase_azimuthal, cabibbo_azimuthal, numerator_azimuthal,
    gravCouplingCoeff_azimuthal, unruhPeriod_eq a⟩

/-! ## §2 — THE HALF-ANGLE CASCADE: the O1 amplitude is the ℍ half-step of the O3 phase. -/

/-- ★ NEW TIE. The O1 fold-phase Born amplitude is the ℍ HALF-STEP of the O3 Cabibbo phase:
    `cutCos foldPhase² = (1 + cutCos(2·foldPhase))/2`. The amplitude-halving law (N416
