    O2 mass-phase amplitude and the O3 mixing phase are ONE cascade step apart. Never banked with
    `2·foldPhase` as the argument. Physics-words-removable: `cutCos(cutPi/8)² = (1+cutCos(cutPi/4))/2`. -/
theorem foldPhase_is_half_of_cabibbo :
    cutCos foldPhase * cutCos foldPhase = (1 + cutCos ((2 : Cut) * foldPhase)) / 2 := by
  rw [twoP_eq_quarter]
  exact foldPhase_amplitude.2

